<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρήορος</span></b> , so in 
			Ep.
		 and 
			Ion.
		, but 
			Dor.
		 and 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράορος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span> (as always in
		Trag.), also 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάρᾱρος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			15.8
		</span></i> : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραείρω</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνήορος</span>) : -<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>joined</i> or <i>hung beside</i> : hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρήορος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>), <i>horse which draws by the side of the
				regular pair</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυνωρίς</span>),
				<i>outrunner</i>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειραφόρος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.471
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				474
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.73
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>lying along, outstretched, sprawling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκειτο π. ἔνθα καὶ ἔνθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.7.156
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀχρεῖον καὶ π. δέμας κεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					365
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> metaph.,
				<i>reckless, senseless</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ τι π. οὐδ᾽ ἀεσίφρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.603
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> l.c. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὄμμα τιταίνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tryph.
					371
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόου παρήορος</span>
			<i>distraught</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				56.5
			</span></i>.</div>
